"""
A key of the server, such as the key of the form tokens, in a file of its
own: never a literal of the programme, never an argument or a variable of
the environment, where it would show in the process list, a shell history
or a log.

The file holds the key as it is used.  makeKey writes a new one: 32 bytes
from the secure random source of libcrypto, as 64 hexadecimal digits, in a
file that is made new with mode 0600 and never replaces one that is there.
readKey takes a file only when it is a regular file that neither its group
nor anyone else may read, write or run, between 32 and 4096 bytes long.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);

module Wolly.Secret is
    """
    The fewest bytes a key may have: 32.
    """
    function keyBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 32;

    """
    The key in the file at path.  None when there is no file, when it is
    not a regular file, when its mode gives its group or others any
    access, when it is shorter than keyBytes or longer than 4096 bytes, and
    when it cannot be read.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [P: Region]
    function readKey(path: Span[Nat8, P]): Option[String];

    """
    Makes the file at path with a new key, mode 0600.  False when
    something is at path already, which is never replaced, when the random
    source fails, and when the file cannot be written.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [P: Region]
    function makeKey(path: Span[Nat8, P]): Bool;
end module.
